    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46570" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Summoenĭum</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Subm-</span></b> ), ii, n.
		submoenia, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a place in Rome</i>, <i>probably near
				the walls</i>, <i>the resort of vile
			characters</i>, <i><span class="en">Mart. 1, 35, 6</span></i>.— Hence,
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Summoenĭānus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Summœnium</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">uxores,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					3, 82, 2</span></i>
			; cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">buccae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					11, 61, 2</span></i>
			.</div>
